meta {
  name: downloadDocument
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/document/get/{{serviceInstanceId}}/{{documentId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  XTM-Hub-User-Platform-Token: {{userPlatformToken}}
  XTM-Hub-Platform-Id: {{platformId}}
  XTM-Hub-Platform-Token: {{platformToken}}
  ~XTM-Hub-Platform-Assertion: {{platformAssertion}}
}

docs {
  Downloads the file of a document (add ?attach=true to get it as an attachment). The user comes from the session
  cookie, or from XTM-Hub-User-Platform-Token for a platform that downloads for its user: without either, 401.

  A platform sends either the assertion header or the token headers:
  - XTM-Hub-Platform-Assertion (disabled here): a JWS signed by the key the platform enrolled, whose htu claim must be
    exactly the path of this request (/document/get/<serviceInstanceId>/<documentId>), so it opens no other document.
    Checked whenever present, and sent once only.
  - XTM-Hub-Platform-Id and XTM-Hub-Platform-Token: checked only with a user platform token and when the platform token
    is present, so that older versions without it keep working. The registration must be active.

  A refused platform answers 403 { "message": "platform registration is not valid" }, with a "code"
  (PLATFORM_ASSERTION_INVALID, PLATFORM_KEY_MISMATCH, PLATFORM_TOKEN_REFUSED) when the assertion or the token of a
  platform that enrolled a key is refused.
}
